
/**
 *
 * Author : Levi Lacoss (fishyfishfish55)
 * Github : @fishyfishfish55
 *
 * Colors
 *
 * Recoloured 2026-09-17 to match the waybar. Only these six names exist -- the
 * whole of config.rasi funnels through them via the `* { ... var(x) }` block, so
 * this file is the entire palette. The two hardcoded blues left in config.rasi
 * (#89B4FA at :69 and #6f91c9 at :91) are inert: both sit on `border: 0px solid`.
 *
 * MAPPING, taken from what the menu actually looked like on screen:
 *   the DARK BLUE window       #20212C -> #2f193d  the waybar bar backdrop
 *   the LIGHT BLUE highlight   #7A95C9 -> #f7bcbc  the waybar pill
 *   the pale blue list text    #C0CAF5 -> #f7bcbc  same pill colour
 *
 * `selected` is both the highlighted row's background AND the mode buttons and
 * scrollbar handle, so pink there reproduces the bar's pink-pill look; its text
 * comes from var(background), giving dark purple on pink exactly like the bar.
 * Unselected rows invert that: pink text on the dark purple window.
 *
 * Contrast, measured: 9.70:1 both ways for normal and selected rows (the old
 * scheme was 9.89:1 normal but only 5.30:1 selected), 8.40:1 on alternate rows.
 **/

* {
    background:     #2f193dFF;
    background-alt: #3d2150FF;
    foreground:     #f7bcbcFF;
    selected:       #f7bcbcFF;

    /* `active` is used as a BACKGROUND with var(background) as its text, so it
       has to be light, not a mid purple -- #6e3a83 here measured 1.96:1 and was
       rejected. This lavender is clearly distinguishable from the pill pink
       while reading at 7.52:1. */
    active:         #c9a6ddFF;

    /* Left alone: amber, not blue, so outside what was asked -- and it is the
       urgent state, which should not blend into the rest of the palette. */
    urgent:         #ECD3A0FF;
}
